{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YZSpMZDKrj8bmLfgYSNXu1","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Implementation Plan: share_docs (Documentation Export)\n     2→\n     3→## Overview\n     4→\n     5→Add a documentation export system to the Vista dashboard that produces a single self-contained HTML file with architecture diagrams (Mermaid) and domain requirements (markdown) for selected features. The exported file works on any device with internet (CDN dependencies), no server required.\n     6→\n     7→## Architecture Summary\n     8→\n     9→```\n    10→project.html ─── \"Export Documentation\" button\n    11→       │\n    12→       ▼\n    13→ Export Modal (JS) ─── GET /api/projects/{id}/export/features\n    14→       │                         │\n    15→       │                         ▼\n    16→       │              ProgressService + ProjectService\n    17→       │              (scan features, diagrams, requirements)\n    18→       │\n    19→       ▼\n    20→ POST /api/projects/{id}/export\n    21→       │\n    22→       ▼\n    23→ ExportService.generate_html()\n    24→       │\n    25→       ├── Read _arch.json manifests\n    26→       ├── Read .mmd diagram sources\n    27→       ├── Read domain-requirements.md\n    28→       └── Render export.html Jinja2 template\n    29→       │\n    30→       ▼\n    31→ StreamingResponse (Content-Disposition: attachment)\n    32→```\n    33→\n    34→---\n    35→\n    36→## Step 1: Add `read_domain_requirements()` to ProgressService\n    37→\n    38→**File:** `vista/server/services/progress_service.py`\n    39→\n    40→Add a new static method to the existing `ProgressService` class:\n    41→\n    42→```python\n    43→@staticmethod\n    44→def read_domain_requirements(project_path: str, feature_name: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    45→    \"\"\"Read domain-requirements.md if it exists.\"\"\"\n    46→    req_file = Path(project_path) / \".vista\" / \"features\" / feature_name / \"domain-requirements.md\"\n    47→    if not req_file.exists():\n    48→        return None\n    49→    try:\n    50→        content = req_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    51→        return content if content.strip() else None\n    52→    except OSError:\n    53→        return None\n    54→```\n    55→\n    56→**Why:** The existing ProgressService has `read_arch_manifest` and `read_arch_file` but nothing for domain requirements. This follows the existing pattern (static methods, path traversal safety via known paths, returns None on missing/empty).\n    57→\n    58→---\n    59→\n    60→## Step 2: Create ExportService\n    61→\n    62→**File:** `vista/server/services/export_service.py` (NEW)\n    63→\n    64→A service class that assembles export data and renders the Jinja2 template.\n    65→\n    66→### Class design:\n    67→\n    68→```python\n    69→class ExportService:\n    70→    @staticmethod\n    71→    def get_exportable_features(project_path: str) -> list[dict]:\n    72→        \"\"\"Return features with their diagrams and requirements availability.\n    73→\n    74→        Returns list of dicts:\n    75→        [\n    76→            {\n    77→                \"name\": \"feature_name\",\n    78→                \"has_requirements\": True,\n    79→                \"diagrams\": [\n    80→                    {\"name\": \"System Architecture\", \"file\": \"system-architecture.mmd\",\n    81→                     \"type\": \"mermaid\", \"description\": \"...\", \"category\": \"architecture\"}\n    82→                ]\n    83→            }\n    84→        ]\n    85→\n    86→        Only features with at least one diagram OR non-empty requirements are included.\n    87→        \"\"\"\n    88→\n    89→    @staticmethod\n    90→    def generate_export_html(\n    91→        project_name: str,\n    92→        project_path: str,\n    93→        selected_features: list[dict],  # [{name: str, diagrams: [str]}]\n    94→    ) -> str:\n    95→        \"\"\"Generate the self-contained HTML export.\n    96→\n    97→        For each selected feature:\n    98→        1. Read _arch.json manifest\n    99→        2. Filter diagrams to only those selected\n   100→        3. Read .mmd content for each selected diagram\n   101→        4. Read domain-requirements.md\n   102→        5. Assemble into template context\n   103→\n   104→        Returns rendered HTML string.\n   105→        \"\"\"\n   106→```\n   107→\n   108→### Key behaviors:\n   109→\n   110→- **`get_exportable_features()`** reuses `ProgressService.read_arch_manifest()` and `ProgressService.read_domain_requirements()` to scan features. Filters out features with no diagrams AND no requirements.\n   111→\n   112→- **`generate_export_html()`** collects data into a template context dict:\n   113→  ```python\n   114→  context = {\n   115→      \"project_name\": project_name,\n   116→      \"export_date\": datetime.now().strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\"),\n   117→      \"features\": [\n   118→          {\n   119→              \"name\": \"feature_name\",\n   120→              \"diagrams\": [\n   121→                  {\"name\": \"...\", \"file\": \"...\", \"description\": \"...\",\n   122→                   \"category\": \"...\", \"content\": \"<mermaid source>\"}\n   123→              ],\n   124→              \"requirements_md\": \"# Domain Requirements...\",  # or None\n   125→          }\n   126→      ]\n   127→  }\n   128→  ```\n   129→  Then renders the `export.html` Jinja2 template with this context.\n   130→\n   131→- **Edge cases:**\n   132→  - Missing `_arch.json` → skip diagrams for that feature, include requirements only\n   133→  - Empty `domain-requirements.md` → skip requirements, include diagrams only\n   134→  - `.mmd` file not found → skip that diagram (log warning)\n   135→  - Corrupt JSON in `_arch.json` → skip entirely (read_arch_manifest returns None)\n   136→\n   137→### Jinja2 template loading:\n   138→\n   139→Use a standalone `jinja2.Environment` with `FileSystemLoader` pointed at `config.VIEWS_DIR`, since this service needs to render a template outside of a FastAPI request context. The existing pattern (routes creating their own `Jinja2Templates` instance) supports this.\n   140→\n   141→---\n   142→\n   143→## Step 3: Create Export Routes\n   144→\n   145→**File:** `vista/server/routes/export.py` (NEW)\n   146→\n   147→### Endpoints:\n   148→\n   149→#### `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/export/features`\n   150→\n   151→Returns the feature tree for the export modal checklist.\n   152→\n   153→```python\n   154→@router.get(\"/api/projects/{project_id}/export/features\")\n   155→async def get_export_features(project_id: str):\n   156→    project = ProjectService.get_by_id(project_id)\n   157→    if not project:\n   158→        raise HTTPException(404, \"Project not found\")\n   159→    features = ExportService.get_exportable_features(project.path)\n   160→    return features\n   161→```\n   162→\n   163→**Response shape:**\n   164→```json\n   165→[\n   166→  {\n   167→    \"name\": \"diagram_representations\",\n   168→    \"has_requirements\": true,\n   169→    \"diagrams\": [\n   170→      {\"name\": \"System Architecture\", \"file\": \"system-architecture.mmd\", \"description\": \"...\", \"category\": \"architecture\"},\n   171→      {\"name\": \"Data Model\", \"file\": \"data-model.mmd\", \"description\": \"...\", \"category\": \"architecture\"}\n   172→    ]\n   173→  }\n   174→]\n   175→```\n   176→\n   177→#### `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/export`\n   178→\n   179→Generates and returns the HTML file.\n   180→\n   181→```python\n   182→from fastapi.responses import Response\n   183→\n   184→@router.post(\"/api/projects/{project_id}/export\")\n   185→async def export_documentation(project_id: str, body: ExportRequest):\n   186→    project = ProjectService.get_by_id(project_id)\n   187→    if not project:\n   188→        raise HTTPException(404, \"Project not found\")\n   189→\n   190→    html = ExportService.generate_export_html(\n   191→        project_name=project.name,\n   192→        project_path=project.path,\n   193→        selected_features=body.features,\n   194→    )\n   195→\n   196→    filename = f\"{project.name}-docs-{datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%d')}.html\"\n   197→\n   198→    return Response(\n   199→        content=html,\n   200→        media_type=\"text/html\",\n   201→        headers={\n   202→            \"Content-Disposition\": f'attachment; filename=\"{filename}\"'\n   203→        }\n   204→    )\n   205→```\n   206→\n   207→**Request body model:**\n   208→```python\n   209→from pydantic import BaseModel\n   210→\n   211→class ExportFeatureSelection(BaseModel):\n   212→    name: str\n   213→    diagrams: list[str]  # list of filenames, e.g. [\"system-architecture.mmd\"]\n   214→\n   215→class ExportRequest(BaseModel):\n   216→    features: list[ExportFeatureSelection]\n   217→```\n   218→\n   219→### Route registration:\n   220→\n   221→Add to `vista/server/app.py`:\n   222→```python\n   223→from server.routes import export\n   224→app.include_router(export.router)\n   225→```\n   226→\n   227→---\n   228→\n   229→## Step 4: Create Export HTML Template\n   230→\n   231→**File:** `vista/server/views/export.html` (NEW)\n   232→\n   233→A **standalone** HTML file (NOT extending `_base.html`) that is self-contained when rendered. This template is rendered server-side by ExportService; the resulting HTML works without any server.\n   234→\n   235→### Template structure:\n   236→\n   237→```html\n   238→<!DOCTYPE html>\n   239→<html lang=\"en\">\n   240→<head>\n   241→    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n   242→    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n   243→    <title>{{ project_name }} - Documentation Export</title>\n   244→    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n   245→    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11/dist/mermaid.min.js\"></script>\n   246→    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/marked@15/marked.min.js\"></script>\n   247→    <style>\n   248→        /* Vista dark theme styles - diagram cards, modal overlay, etc. */\n   249→        /* Reuse key CSS from architecture.html: diagram-card, diagram-body,\n   250→           diagram-viewport, zoom controls, modal overlay */\n   251→    </style>\n   252→</head>\n   253→<body class=\"bg-gray-900 text-gray-100 min-h-screen\">\n   254→    <!-- Header -->\n   255→    <header>\n   256→        Vista Dashboard · {{ project_name }} · Exported {{ export_date }}\n   257→    </header>\n   258→\n   259→    <!-- Feature Navigation (if multiple features) -->\n   260→    {% if features|length > 1 %}\n   261→    <nav>\n   262→        {% for feature in features %}\n   263→        <a href=\"#feature-{{ feature.name }}\">{{ feature.name }}</a>\n   264→        {% endfor %}\n   265→    </nav>\n   266→    {% endif %}\n   267→\n   268→    <!-- Feature Sections -->\n   269→    {% for feature in features %}\n   270→    <section id=\"feature-{{ feature.name }}\">\n   271→        <h2>{{ feature.name }}</h2>\n   272→\n   273→        <!-- Diagram Card Gallery -->\n   274→        {% for diagram in feature.diagrams %}\n   275→        <div class=\"diagram-card\" data-idx=\"{{ loop.index }}\">\n   276→            <div class=\"diagram-header\">\n   277→                <span>{{ diagram.name }}</span>\n   278→                <span class=\"badge\">{{ diagram.category }}</span>\n   279→            </div>\n   280→            <div class=\"diagram-body\">\n   281→                <div class=\"diagram-viewport\">\n   282→                    <div class=\"mermaid\" id=\"mermaid-{{ feature.name }}-{{ loop.index }}\">\n   283→                        {{ diagram.content }}\n   284→                    </div>\n   285→                </div>\n   286→                <div class=\"diagram-zoom-controls\">\n   287→                    <!-- zoom buttons -->\n   288→                </div>\n   289→            </div>\n   290→        </div>\n   291→        {% endfor %}\n   292→\n   293→        <!-- Domain Requirements -->\n   294→        {% if feature.requirements_md %}\n   295→        <div class=\"requirements-section\" id=\"requirements-{{ feature.name }}\">\n   296→            <!-- rendered client-side via marked.js -->\n   297→        </div>\n   298→        {% endif %}\n   299→    </section>\n   300→    {% endfor %}\n   301→\n   302→    <!-- Modal Overlay (for expanded diagram view) -->\n   303→    <div id=\"diagram-modal\" class=\"modal-overlay\" style=\"display:none;\">\n   304→        <!-- Full-screen diagram viewer with zoom/pan -->\n   305→    </div>\n   306→\n   307→    <script>\n   308→        // Mermaid initialization (dark theme)\n   309→        mermaid.initialize({ startOnLoad: true, theme: 'dark', ... });\n   310→\n   311→        // Render requirements markdown via marked.js\n   312→        // Pan/zoom for diagram cards\n   313→        // Modal expand/close logic\n   314→        // Feature nav scroll\n   315→    </script>\n   316→</body>\n   317→</html>\n   318→```\n   319→\n   320→### Key CSS to extract from existing templates:\n   321→\n   322→From `architecture.html`:\n   323→- `.diagram-card`, `.diagram-header`, `.diagram-body`, `.diagram-viewport` (card gallery styling)\n   324→- `.diagram-zoom-controls` (zoom buttons)\n   325→- `.badge`, `.badge-arch`, `.badge-tdd` (category badges)\n   326→- Mermaid SVG visibility overrides (stroke-width, font-size)\n   327→\n   328→From `diagram_expand.html`:\n   329→- Full-screen modal overlay pattern (toolbar + diagram area + pan/zoom)\n   330→\n   331→### Key JavaScript to include:\n   332→\n   333→- Mermaid init (dark theme variables — copy from architecture.html)\n   334→- `marked.setOptions({ breaks: true, gfm: true })` + render requirements sections\n   335→- Pan/zoom handlers for each diagram card (simplified version of architecture.html's initViewport)\n   336→- Modal open/close: clicking a card opens the modal with that diagram full-screen\n   337→- Feature navigation: smooth scroll to anchors\n   338→\n   339→### Template data contract:\n   340→\n   341→The Jinja2 template receives:\n   342→```python\n   343→{\n   344→    \"project_name\": str,\n   345→    \"export_date\": str,  # \"YYYY-MM-DD\"\n   346→    \"features\": [\n   347→        {\n   348→            \"name\": str,\n   349→            \"diagrams\": [\n   350→                {\n   351→                    \"name\": str,\n   352→                    \"file\": str,\n   353→                    \"description\": str,\n   354→                    \"category\": str,  # \"architecture\" or \"tdd\"\n   355→                    \"content\": str    # raw .mmd source\n   356→                }\n   357→            ],\n   358→            \"requirements_md\": str | None  # raw markdown\n   359→        }\n   360→    ]\n   361→}\n   362→```\n   363→\n   364→---\n   365→\n   366→## Step 5: Add Export Modal to Project Page\n   367→\n   368→**File:** `vista/server/views/project.html` (MODIFY)\n   369→\n   370→### UI changes:\n   371→\n   372→1. **Add \"Export Documentation\" button** next to the existing \"Remove Project\" button in the project header:\n   373→   ```html\n   374→   <button onclick=\"openExportModal()\"\n   375→           class=\"px-3 py-1.5 rounded border border-blue-600 text-blue-300 hover:bg-blue-900/30 text-sm transition-colors\">\n   376→       Export Documentation\n   377→   </button>\n   378→   ```\n   379→\n   380→2. **Add Export Modal HTML** (hidden by default) at the bottom of the content block:\n   381→   ```html\n   382→   <!-- Export Modal -->\n   383→   <div id=\"export-modal\" class=\"fixed inset-0 bg-black/60 z-50 hidden flex items-center justify-center\">\n   384→       <div class=\"bg-gray-800 rounded-lg border border-gray-700 w-full max-w-lg max-h-[80vh] flex flex-col\">\n   385→           <div class=\"px-4 py-3 border-b border-gray-700 flex items-center justify-between\">\n   386→               <h3 class=\"font-semibold\">Export Documentation</h3>\n   387→               <button onclick=\"closeExportModal()\">✕</button>\n   388→           </div>\n   389→\n   390→           <div class=\"flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-4\" id=\"export-tree\">\n   391→               <!-- Loading / Tree / Error states -->\n   392→           </div>\n   393→\n   394→           <div class=\"px-4 py-3 border-t border-gray-700 flex items-center justify-between\">\n   395→               <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n   396→                   <button onclick=\"selectAllExport(true)\" class=\"text-xs text-blue-400\">Select All</button>\n   397→                   <button onclick=\"selectAllExport(false)\" class=\"text-xs text-gray-400\">Deselect All</button>\n   398→               </div>\n   399→               <button id=\"export-download-btn\" onclick=\"startExport()\" disabled\n   400→                       class=\"px-4 py-2 rounded bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-500 text-sm font-medium disabled:opacity-40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed\">\n   401→                   Download\n   402→               </button>\n   403→           </div>\n   404→       </div>\n   405→   </div>\n   406→   ```\n   407→\n   408→3. **Add JavaScript** in the `{% block scripts %}` section:\n   409→\n   410→### JavaScript behavior:\n   411→\n   412→```javascript\n   413→// State\n   414→let exportFeatures = [];\n   415→\n   416→async function openExportModal() {\n   417→    document.getElementById('export-modal').classList.remove('hidden');\n   418→    document.getElementById('export-tree').innerHTML = '<div class=\"text-gray-500 text-center py-8\">Loading features...</div>';\n   419→\n   420→    try {\n   421→        const resp = await fetch(`/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/export/features`);\n   422→        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error('Failed to load features');\n   423→        exportFeatures = await resp.json();\n   424→\n   425→        if (exportFeatures.length === 0) {\n   426→            document.getElementById('export-tree').innerHTML =\n   427→                '<div class=\"text-gray-500 text-center py-8\">No exportable features found</div>';\n   428→            return;\n   429→        }\n   430→\n   431→        renderExportTree();\n   432→    } catch (err) {\n   433→        document.getElementById('export-tree').innerHTML =\n   434→            `<div class=\"text-red-400 text-center py-8\">${err.message}</div>`;\n   435→    }\n   436→}\n   437→\n   438→function renderExportTree() {\n   439→    // For each feature: expandable parent with checkbox\n   440→    //   Children: individual diagram checkboxes\n   441→    // Feature checkbox toggles all children\n   442→    // Individual diagram checkboxes update parent state (checked, indeterminate, unchecked)\n   443→}\n   444→\n   445→function updateDownloadButton() {\n   446→    // Enable if at least one diagram or feature-with-requirements is selected\n   447→    // Disable otherwise with tooltip\n   448→}\n   449→\n   450→async function startExport() {\n   451→    // Collect selected features + diagrams from checkboxes\n   452→    // POST to /api/projects/{id}/export\n   453→    // Trigger download via blob URL + click trick\n   454→    // Show loading spinner during generation\n   455→    // Show toast on error\n   456→}\n   457→\n   458→function closeExportModal() {\n   459→    document.getElementById('export-modal').classList.add('hidden');\n   460→}\n   461→```\n   462→\n   463→### Tree checklist UX:\n   464→\n   465→- Each feature row has: expand/collapse chevron, checkbox, feature name, diagram count badge\n   466→- Expanded: shows each diagram with checkbox, name, and description\n   467→- Feature checkbox behavior:\n   468→  - Checked → all diagrams checked\n   469→  - Unchecked → all diagrams unchecked\n   470→  - Indeterminate → some diagrams checked (via individual toggles)\n   471→- Requirements are implicitly included when any content from a feature is selected (no separate checkbox)\n   472→\n   473→### Download mechanism:\n   474→\n   475→```javascript\n   476→async function startExport() {\n   477→    const btn = document.getElementById('export-download-btn');\n   478→    btn.disabled = true;\n   479→    btn.textContent = 'Generating...';\n   480→\n   481→    const selected = collectSelectedFeatures(); // [{name, diagrams: [filenames]}]\n   482→\n   483→    try {\n   484→        const resp = await fetch(`/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/export`, {\n   485→            method: 'POST',\n   486→            headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n   487→            body: JSON.stringify({ features: selected }),\n   488→        });\n   489→\n   490→        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error('Export failed');\n   491→\n   492→        const blob = await resp.blob();\n   493→        const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);\n   494→        const a = document.createElement('a');\n   495→        a.href = url;\n   496→        a.download = resp.headers.get('Content-Disposition')?.match(/filename=\"(.+)\"/)?.[1]\n   497→                     || 'export.html';\n   498→        document.body.appendChild(a);\n   499→        a.click();\n   500→        a.remove();\n   501→        URL.revokeObjectURL(url);\n   502→\n   503→        closeExportModal();\n   504→    } catch (err) {\n   505→        // Show error toast\n   506→    } finally {\n   507→        btn.disabled = false;\n   508→        btn.textContent = 'Download';\n   509→    }\n   510→}\n   511→```\n   512→\n   513→---\n   514→\n   515→## Step 6: Tests\n   516→\n   517→**File:** `vista/tests/test_export_service.py` (NEW)\n   518→\n   519→### Test cases for ExportService:\n   520→\n   521→1. **`test_get_exportable_features_returns_features_with_diagrams`** — project with features that have `_arch.json` manifests\n   522→2. **`test_get_exportable_features_excludes_empty_features`** — feature with no diagrams and no requirements is excluded\n   523→3. **`test_get_exportable_features_includes_requirements_only_features`** — feature with no diagrams but valid `domain-requirements.md` is included\n   524→4. **`test_generate_export_html_basic`** — generates valid HTML with one feature, one diagram\n   525→5. **`test_generate_export_html_multiple_features`** — generates HTML with navigation when >1 feature\n   526→6. **`test_generate_export_html_missing_diagram_file`** — gracefully skips missing .mmd files\n   527→7. **`test_generate_export_html_missing_manifest`** — includes requirements when manifest is missing\n   528→8. **`test_generate_export_html_empty_requirements`** — skips requirements section when domain-requirements.md is empty\n   529→\n   530→### Test cases for routes:\n   531→\n   532→9. **`test_get_export_features_endpoint`** — returns correct JSON shape\n   533→10. **`test_post_export_endpoint`** — returns HTML with correct Content-Disposition header\n   534→11. **`test_post_export_invalid_project`** — returns 404\n   535→\n   536→### Test approach:\n   537→\n   538→Use `tmp_path` fixture to create mock `.vista/features/` directories with test manifests and .mmd files. Follow existing test patterns from `vista/tests/test_ralph_service.py`.\n   539→\n   540→---\n   541→\n   542→## File Summary\n   543→\n   544→| Action | File | Description |\n   545→|--------|------|-------------|\n   546→| MODIFY | `vista/server/services/progress_service.py` | Add `read_domain_requirements()` method |\n   547→| CREATE | `vista/server/services/export_service.py` | ExportService with `get_exportable_features()` and `generate_export_html()` |\n   548→| CREATE | `vista/server/routes/export.py` | Two API endpoints: GET features, POST export |\n   549→| MODIFY | `vista/server/app.py` | Register export router |\n   550→| CREATE | `vista/server/views/export.html` | Self-contained export template |\n   551→| MODIFY | `vista/server/views/project.html` | Add Export button + modal |\n   552→| CREATE | `vista/tests/test_export_service.py` | Unit tests for export service and routes |\n   553→\n   554→---\n   555→\n   556→## Dependencies\n   557→\n   558→- **No new Python packages** — uses existing `jinja2` (already a FastAPI dependency), `pathlib`, `json`, `datetime`\n   559→- **No new CDN links in dashboard** — the export template uses CDN links but those are only in the exported HTML output\n   560→- **Reuses existing services**: `ProjectService.get_by_id()`, `ProgressService.read_arch_manifest()`, `ProgressService.read_arch_file()`\n   561→\n   562→## Risks & Mitigations\n   563→\n   564→| Risk | Mitigation |\n   565→|------|-----------|\n   566→| Large export files (many diagrams) | Mermaid source is typically <5KB per diagram; 20 diagrams ≈ 100KB. Template HTML/CSS/JS overhead ≈ 50KB. Well within 500KB target. |\n   567→| Mermaid rendering failures in export | The export embeds raw Mermaid source that renders client-side. If a diagram has parse errors, Mermaid shows an error inline — same behavior as the dashboard. |\n   568→| Path traversal in diagram filenames | Reuse `ProgressService.read_arch_file()` which already has path traversal prevention. |\n   569→| Stale CDN libraries | Pin to major versions (@11, @15) to avoid breaking changes while getting patches. |\n   570→\n   571→## Implementation Order\n   572→\n   573→1. Step 1 (ProgressService) — 5 min, enables step 2\n   574→2. Step 2 (ExportService) — core logic, ~30 min\n   575→3. Step 3 (Routes) — thin layer over service, ~10 min\n   576→4. Step 4 (Export template) — most effort: HTML/CSS/JS, ~45 min\n   577→5. Step 5 (Project page modal) — UI integration, ~30 min\n   578→6. Step 6 (Tests) — ~20 min\n   579→\n   580→Steps 2+3 can be built and tested via API before the UI (steps 4+5) is complete.\n   581→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1bdbba0f-99f5-433c-bb72-957fe6bd9616","uuid":"98b0e7c7-db36-4973-956f-322c583c7a9a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/ralph/share-docs-plan/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","content":"# Implementation Plan: share_docs (Documentation Export)\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd a documentation export system to the Vista dashboard that produces a single self-contained HTML file with architecture diagrams (Mermaid) and domain requirements (markdown) for selected features. The exported file works on any device with internet (CDN dependencies), no server required.\n\n## Architecture Summary\n\n```\nproject.html ─── \"Export Documentation\" button\n       │\n       ▼\n Export Modal (JS) ─── GET /api/projects/{id}/export/features\n       │                         │\n       │                         ▼\n       │              ProgressService + ProjectService\n       │              (scan features, diagrams, requirements)\n       │\n       ▼\n POST /api/projects/{id}/export\n       │\n       ▼\n ExportService.generate_html()\n       │\n       ├── Read _arch.json manifests\n       ├── Read .mmd diagram sources\n       ├── Read domain-requirements.md\n       └── Render export.html Jinja2 template\n       │\n       ▼\n StreamingResponse (Content-Disposition: attachment)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Add `read_domain_requirements()` to ProgressService\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/progress_service.py`\n\nAdd a new static method to the existing `ProgressService` class:\n\n```python\n@staticmethod\ndef read_domain_requirements(project_path: str, feature_name: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"Read domain-requirements.md if it exists.\"\"\"\n    req_file = Path(project_path) / \".vista\" / \"features\" / feature_name / \"domain-requirements.md\"\n    if not req_file.exists():\n        return None\n    try:\n        content = req_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        return content if content.strip() else None\n    except OSError:\n        return None\n```\n\n**Why:** The existing ProgressService has `read_arch_manifest` and `read_arch_file` but nothing for domain requirements. This follows the existing pattern (static methods, path traversal safety via known paths, returns None on missing/empty).\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Create ExportService\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/export_service.py` (NEW)\n\nA service class that assembles export data and renders the Jinja2 template.\n\n### Class design:\n\n```python\nclass ExportService:\n    @staticmethod\n    def get_exportable_features(project_path: str) -> list[dict]:\n        \"\"\"Return features with their diagrams and requirements availability.\n\n        Returns list of dicts:\n        [\n            {\n                \"name\": \"feature_name\",\n                \"has_requirements\": True,\n                \"diagrams\": [\n                    {\"name\": \"System Architecture\", \"file\": \"system-architecture.mmd\",\n                     \"type\": \"mermaid\", \"description\": \"...\", \"category\": \"architecture\"}\n                ]\n            }\n        ]\n\n        Only features with at least one diagram OR non-empty requirements are included.\n        \"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def generate_export_html(\n        project_name: str,\n        project_path: str,\n        selected_features: list[dict],  # [{name: str, diagrams: [str]}]\n    ) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Generate the self-contained HTML export.\n\n        For each selected feature:\n        1. Read _arch.json manifest\n        2. Filter diagrams to only those selected\n        3. Read .mmd content for each selected diagram\n        4. Read domain-requirements.md\n        5. Assemble into template context\n\n        Returns rendered HTML string.\n        \"\"\"\n```\n\n### Key behaviors:\n\n- **`get_exportable_features()`** reuses `ProgressService.read_arch_manifest()` and `ProgressService.read_domain_requirements()` to scan features. Filters out features with no diagrams AND no requirements.\n\n- **`generate_export_html()`** collects data into a template context dict:\n  ```python\n  context = {\n      \"project_name\": project_name,\n      \"export_date\": datetime.now().strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\"),\n      \"features\": [\n          {\n              \"name\": \"feature_name\",\n              \"diagrams\": [\n                  {\"name\": \"...\", \"file\": \"...\", \"description\": \"...\",\n                   \"category\": \"...\", \"content\": \"<mermaid source>\"}\n              ],\n              \"requirements_md\": \"# Domain Requirements...\",  # or None\n          }\n      ]\n  }\n  ```\n  Then renders the `export.html` Jinja2 template with this context.\n\n- **Edge cases:**\n  - Missing `_arch.json` → skip diagrams for that feature, include requirements only\n  - Empty `domain-requirements.md` → skip requirements, include diagrams only\n  - `.mmd` file not found → skip that diagram (log warning)\n  - Corrupt JSON in `_arch.json` → skip entirely (read_arch_manifest returns None)\n\n### Jinja2 template loading:\n\nUse a standalone `jinja2.Environment` with `FileSystemLoader` pointed at `config.VIEWS_DIR`, since this service needs to render a template outside of a FastAPI request context. The existing pattern (routes creating their own `Jinja2Templates` instance) supports this.\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Create Export Routes\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/export.py` (NEW)\n\n### Endpoints:\n\n#### `GET /api/projects/{project_id}/export/features`\n\nReturns the feature tree for the export modal checklist.\n\n```python\n@router.get(\"/api/projects/{project_id}/export/features\")\nasync def get_export_features(project_id: str):\n    project = ProjectService.get_by_id(project_id)\n    if not project:\n        raise HTTPException(404, \"Project not found\")\n    features = ExportService.get_exportable_features(project.path)\n    return features\n```\n\n**Response shape:**\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"diagram_representations\",\n    \"has_requirements\": true,\n    \"diagrams\": [\n      {\"name\": \"System Architecture\", \"file\": \"system-architecture.mmd\", \"description\": \"...\", \"category\": \"architecture\"},\n      {\"name\": \"Data Model\", \"file\": \"data-model.mmd\", \"description\": \"...\", \"category\": \"architecture\"}\n    ]\n  }\n]\n```\n\n#### `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/export`\n\nGenerates and returns the HTML file.\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi.responses import Response\n\n@router.post(\"/api/projects/{project_id}/export\")\nasync def export_documentation(project_id: str, body: ExportRequest):\n    project = ProjectService.get_by_id(project_id)\n    if not project:\n        raise HTTPException(404, \"Project not found\")\n\n    html = ExportService.generate_export_html(\n        project_name=project.name,\n        project_path=project.path,\n        selected_features=body.features,\n    )\n\n    filename = f\"{project.name}-docs-{datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%d')}.html\"\n\n    return Response(\n        content=html,\n        media_type=\"text/html\",\n        headers={\n            \"Content-Disposition\": f'attachment; filename=\"{filename}\"'\n        }\n    )\n```\n\n**Request body model:**\n```python\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\nclass ExportFeatureSelection(BaseModel):\n    name: str\n    diagrams: list[str]  # list of filenames, e.g. [\"system-architecture.mmd\"]\n\nclass ExportRequest(BaseModel):\n    features: list[ExportFeatureSelection]\n```\n\n### Route registration:\n\nAdd to `vista/server/app.py`:\n```python\nfrom server.routes import export\napp.include_router(export.router)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Create Export HTML Template\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/export.html` (NEW)\n\nA **standalone** HTML file (NOT extending `_base.html`) that is self-contained when rendered. This template is rendered server-side by ExportService; the resulting HTML works without any server.\n\n### Template structure:\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>{{ project_name }} - Documentation Export</title>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11/dist/mermaid.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/marked@15/marked.min.js\"></script>\n    <style>\n        /* Vista dark theme styles - diagram cards, modal overlay, etc. */\n        /* Reuse key CSS from architecture.html: diagram-card, diagram-body,\n           diagram-viewport, zoom controls, modal overlay */\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body class=\"bg-gray-900 text-gray-100 min-h-screen\">\n    <!-- Header -->\n    <header>\n        Vista Dashboard · {{ project_name }} · Exported {{ export_date }}\n    </header>\n\n    <!-- Feature Navigation (if multiple features) -->\n    {% if features|length > 1 %}\n    <nav>\n        {% for feature in features %}\n        <a href=\"#feature-{{ feature.name }}\">{{ feature.name }}</a>\n        {% endfor %}\n    </nav>\n    {% endif %}\n\n    <!-- Feature Sections -->\n    {% for feature in features %}\n    <section id=\"feature-{{ feature.name }}\">\n        <h2>{{ feature.name }}</h2>\n\n        <!-- Diagram Card Gallery -->\n        {% for diagram in feature.diagrams %}\n        <div class=\"diagram-card\" data-idx=\"{{ loop.index }}\">\n            <div class=\"diagram-header\">\n                <span>{{ diagram.name }}</span>\n                <span class=\"badge\">{{ diagram.category }}</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"diagram-body\">\n                <div class=\"diagram-viewport\">\n                    <div class=\"mermaid\" id=\"mermaid-{{ feature.name }}-{{ loop.index }}\">\n                        {{ diagram.content }}\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"diagram-zoom-controls\">\n                    <!-- zoom buttons -->\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n        {% endfor %}\n\n        <!-- Domain Requirements -->\n        {% if feature.requirements_md %}\n        <div class=\"requirements-section\" id=\"requirements-{{ feature.name }}\">\n            <!-- rendered client-side via marked.js -->\n        </div>\n        {% endif %}\n    </section>\n    {% endfor %}\n\n    <!-- Modal Overlay (for expanded diagram view) -->\n    <div id=\"diagram-modal\" class=\"modal-overlay\" style=\"display:none;\">\n        <!-- Full-screen diagram viewer with zoom/pan -->\n    </div>\n\n    <script>\n        // Mermaid initialization (dark theme)\n        mermaid.initialize({ startOnLoad: true, theme: 'dark', ... });\n\n        // Render requirements markdown via marked.js\n        // Pan/zoom for diagram cards\n        // Modal expand/close logic\n        // Feature nav scroll\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n### Key CSS to extract from existing templates:\n\nFrom `architecture.html`:\n- `.diagram-card`, `.diagram-header`, `.diagram-body`, `.diagram-viewport` (card gallery styling)\n- `.diagram-zoom-controls` (zoom buttons)\n- `.badge`, `.badge-arch`, `.badge-tdd` (category badges)\n- Mermaid SVG visibility overrides (stroke-width, font-size)\n\nFrom `diagram_expand.html`:\n- Full-screen modal overlay pattern (toolbar + diagram area + pan/zoom)\n\n### Key JavaScript to include:\n\n- Mermaid init (dark theme variables — copy from architecture.html)\n- `marked.setOptions({ breaks: true, gfm: true })` + render requirements sections\n- Pan/zoom handlers for each diagram card (simplified version of architecture.html's initViewport)\n- Modal open/close: clicking a card opens the modal with that diagram full-screen\n- Feature navigation: smooth scroll to anchors\n\n### Template data contract:\n\nThe Jinja2 template receives:\n```python\n{\n    \"project_name\": str,\n    \"export_date\": str,  # \"YYYY-MM-DD\"\n    \"features\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": str,\n            \"diagrams\": [\n                {\n                    \"name\": str,\n                    \"file\": str,\n                    \"description\": str,\n                    \"category\": str,  # \"architecture\" or \"tdd\"\n                    \"content\": str    # raw .mmd source\n                }\n            ],\n            \"requirements_md\": str | None  # raw markdown\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: Add Export Modal to Project Page\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/project.html` (MODIFY)\n\n### UI changes:\n\n1. **Add \"Export Documentation\" button** next to the existing \"Remove Project\" button in the project header:\n   ```html\n   <button onclick=\"openExportModal()\"\n           class=\"px-3 py-1.5 rounded border border-blue-600 text-blue-300 hover:bg-blue-900/30 text-sm transition-colors\">\n       Export Documentation\n   </button>\n   ```\n\n2. **Add Export Modal HTML** (hidden by default) at the bottom of the content block:\n   ```html\n   <!-- Export Modal -->\n   <div id=\"export-modal\" class=\"fixed inset-0 bg-black/60 z-50 hidden flex items-center justify-center\">\n       <div class=\"bg-gray-800 rounded-lg border border-gray-700 w-full max-w-lg max-h-[80vh] flex flex-col\">\n           <div class=\"px-4 py-3 border-b border-gray-700 flex items-center justify-between\">\n               <h3 class=\"font-semibold\">Export Documentation</h3>\n               <button onclick=\"closeExportModal()\">✕</button>\n           </div>\n\n           <div class=\"flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-4\" id=\"export-tree\">\n               <!-- Loading / Tree / Error states -->\n           </div>\n\n           <div class=\"px-4 py-3 border-t border-gray-700 flex items-center justify-between\">\n               <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n                   <button onclick=\"selectAllExport(true)\" class=\"text-xs text-blue-400\">Select All</button>\n                   <button onclick=\"selectAllExport(false)\" class=\"text-xs text-gray-400\">Deselect All</button>\n               </div>\n               <button id=\"export-download-btn\" onclick=\"startExport()\" disabled\n                       class=\"px-4 py-2 rounded bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-500 text-sm font-medium disabled:opacity-40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed\">\n                   Download\n               </button>\n           </div>\n       </div>\n   </div>\n   ```\n\n3. **Add JavaScript** in the `{% block scripts %}` section:\n\n### JavaScript behavior:\n\n```javascript\n// State\nlet exportFeatures = [];\n\nasync function openExportModal() {\n    document.getElementById('export-modal').classList.remove('hidden');\n    document.getElementById('export-tree').innerHTML = '<div class=\"text-gray-500 text-center py-8\">Loading features...</div>';\n\n    try {\n        const resp = await fetch(`/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/export/features`);\n        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error('Failed to load features');\n        exportFeatures = await resp.json();\n\n        if (exportFeatures.length === 0) {\n            document.getElementById('export-tree').innerHTML =\n                '<div class=\"text-gray-500 text-center py-8\">No exportable features found</div>';\n            return;\n        }\n\n        renderExportTree();\n    } catch (err) {\n        document.getElementById('export-tree').innerHTML =\n            `<div class=\"text-red-400 text-center py-8\">${err.message}</div>`;\n    }\n}\n\nfunction renderExportTree() {\n    // For each feature: expandable parent with checkbox\n    //   Children: individual diagram checkboxes\n    // Feature checkbox toggles all children\n    // Individual diagram checkboxes update parent state (checked, indeterminate, unchecked)\n}\n\nfunction updateDownloadButton() {\n    // Enable if at least one diagram or feature-with-requirements is selected\n    // Disable otherwise with tooltip\n}\n\nasync function startExport() {\n    // Collect selected features + diagrams from checkboxes\n    // POST to /api/projects/{id}/export\n    // Trigger download via blob URL + click trick\n    // Show loading spinner during generation\n    // Show toast on error\n}\n\nfunction closeExportModal() {\n    document.getElementById('export-modal').classList.add('hidden');\n}\n```\n\n### Tree checklist UX:\n\n- Each feature row has: expand/collapse chevron, checkbox, feature name, diagram count badge\n- Expanded: shows each diagram with checkbox, name, and description\n- Feature checkbox behavior:\n  - Checked → all diagrams checked\n  - Unchecked → all diagrams unchecked\n  - Indeterminate → some diagrams checked (via individual toggles)\n- Requirements are implicitly included when any content from a feature is selected (no separate checkbox)\n\n### Download mechanism:\n\n```javascript\nasync function startExport() {\n    const btn = document.getElementById('export-download-btn');\n    btn.disabled = true;\n    btn.textContent = 'Generating...';\n\n    const selected = collectSelectedFeatures(); // [{name, diagrams: [filenames]}]\n\n    try {\n        const resp = await fetch(`/api/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/export`, {\n            method: 'POST',\n            headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n            body: JSON.stringify({ features: selected }),\n        });\n\n        if (!resp.ok) throw new Error('Export failed');\n\n        const blob = await resp.blob();\n        const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);\n        const a = document.createElement('a');\n        a.href = url;\n        a.download = resp.headers.get('Content-Disposition')?.match(/filename=\"(.+)\"/)?.[1]\n                     || 'export.html';\n        document.body.appendChild(a);\n        a.click();\n        a.remove();\n        URL.revokeObjectURL(url);\n\n        closeExportModal();\n    } catch (err) {\n        // Show error toast\n    } finally {\n        btn.disabled = false;\n        btn.textContent = 'Download';\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_export_service.py` (NEW)\n\n### Test cases for ExportService:\n\n1. **`test_get_exportable_features_returns_features_with_diagrams`** — project with features that have `_arch.json` manifests\n2. **`test_get_exportable_features_excludes_empty_features`** — feature with no diagrams and no requirements is excluded\n3. **`test_get_exportable_features_includes_requirements_only_features`** — feature with no diagrams but valid `domain-requirements.md` is included\n4. **`test_generate_export_html_basic`** — generates valid HTML with one feature, one diagram\n5. **`test_generate_export_html_multiple_features`** — generates HTML with navigation when >1 feature\n6. **`test_generate_export_html_missing_diagram_file`** — gracefully skips missing .mmd files\n7. **`test_generate_export_html_missing_manifest`** — includes requirements when manifest is missing\n8. **`test_generate_export_html_empty_requirements`** — skips requirements section when domain-requirements.md is empty\n\n### Test cases for routes:\n\n9. **`test_get_export_features_endpoint`** — returns correct JSON shape\n10. **`test_post_export_endpoint`** — returns HTML with correct Content-Disposition header\n11. **`test_post_export_invalid_project`** — returns 404\n\n### Test approach:\n\nUse `tmp_path` fixture to create mock `.vista/features/` directories with test manifests and .mmd files. Follow existing test patterns from `vista/tests/test_ralph_service.py`.\n\n---\n\n## File Summary\n\n| Action | File | Description |\n|--------|------|-------------|\n| MODIFY | `vista/server/services/progress_service.py` | Add `read_domain_requirements()` method |\n| CREATE | `vista/server/services/export_service.py` | ExportService with `get_exportable_features()` and `generate_export_html()` |\n| CREATE | `vista/server/routes/export.py` | Two API endpoints: GET features, POST export |\n| MODIFY | `vista/server/app.py` | Register export router |\n| CREATE | `vista/server/views/export.html` | Self-contained export template |\n| MODIFY | `vista/server/views/project.html` | Add Export button + modal |\n| CREATE | `vista/tests/test_export_service.py` | Unit tests for export service and routes |\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- **No new Python packages** — uses existing `jinja2` (already a FastAPI dependency), `pathlib`, `json`, `datetime`\n- **No new CDN links in dashboard** — the export template uses CDN links but those are only in the exported HTML output\n- **Reuses existing services**: `ProjectService.get_by_id()`, `ProgressService.read_arch_manifest()`, `ProgressService.read_arch_file()`\n\n## Risks & Mitigations\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|------|-----------|\n| Large export files (many diagrams) | Mermaid source is typically <5KB per diagram; 20 diagrams ≈ 100KB. Template HTML/CSS/JS overhead ≈ 50KB. Well within 500KB target. |\n| Mermaid rendering failures in export | The export embeds raw Mermaid source that renders client-side. If a diagram has parse errors, Mermaid shows an error inline — same behavior as the dashboard. |\n| Path traversal in diagram filenames | Reuse `ProgressService.read_arch_file()` which already has path traversal prevention. |\n| Stale CDN libraries | Pin to major versions (@11, @15) to avoid breaking changes while getting patches. |\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n1. Step 1 (ProgressService) — 5 min, enables step 2\n2. Step 2 (ExportService) — core logic, ~30 min\n3. Step 3 (Routes) — thin layer over service, ~10 min\n4. Step 4 (Export template) — most effort: HTML/CSS/JS, ~45 min\n5. Step 5 (Project page modal) — UI integration, ~30 min\n6. Step 6 (Tests) — ~20 min\n\nSteps 2+3 can be built and tested via API before the UI (steps 4+5) is complete.\n","numLines":581,"startLine":1,"totalLines":581}}}
